{
  "id": "miro",
  "name": "Miro",
  "kind": "app",
  "category": "Creative",
  "match": {
    "windows_exe": [
      "Miro.exe"
    ],
    "macos_bundle": [
      "com.electron.realtimeboard"
    ],
    "window_title": [
      "Miro"
    ]
  },
  "sources": [
    "https://help.miro.com/hc/en-us/articles/360017731033-Shortcuts-and-hotkeys",
    "https://help.miro.com/hc/en-us/articles/34307373858450-Presentation-mode"
  ],
  "note": "Covers both the Miro website and the Miro desktop app (same keymap per the vendor's shortcuts article). Not expressible, so left out: duplicate via Alt/Option+drag, select multiple items via Ctrl/Cmd+click, move canvas via Space+drag (all mouse-drag), and 'Move between toolbar items' in Toolbar navigation (vendor lists only 'Arrow keys' without saying which direction moves which way). The single vendor row 'duplicate horizontally or vertically' (Alt/Option+Left/Right/Up/Down) was split into four directional actions since the grammar allows only one key per chord. 'Bring forward' and 'Send backward' now include their Mac binding (Shift+Fn+Up / Shift+Fn+Down, the vendor's only Mac chord for them), since the chord grammar accepts Fn as a mac-only modifier (unlike 'Bring to front'/'Send to back', which also list a plain PageUp/PageDown alternative on Mac).Presentation mode's own article (second source) says only 'use your keyboard arrow keys' to navigate slides without specifying which key advances vs. goes back, and names no chord to enter/exit presentation mode beyond clicking Present/Stop, so no presentation-mode shortcuts are listed here. Desktop app section shortcuts (reload/close tab, exit app, copy board link) only apply to the Windows/Mac desktop app, not the website.",
